```python
def handle_order_placed_unsafe(event):
    inventory.decrement(event.sku, event.qty)      # runs again on redelivery: double-decrements

def handle_order_placed_safe(event):
    if dedup_store.already_processed(event.id):
        return
    inventory.decrement(event.sku, event.qty)
    dedup_store.record(event.id)
```
Both handlers process the identical redelivered event. The unsafe one silently corrupts inventory on the second delivery; the safe one, doing barely more work, produces the correct result no matter how many times the broker redelivers it.
